# Giant Beaver: "Whenever this creature attacks while saddled, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature that saddled it this turn" (CR 702.171b, 115.1, 122.1a); Saddle 3
# (CR 702.171a) needs total power 3 from other creatures. Turn 1: a Black Lotus and a Mox Emerald pay for the Beaver ({3}{G}); four Memnites come down.
# Turn 3: two Memnites (power 2) are refused as saddlers, three can; the fourth Memnite did not saddle it, so it is not a legal target (a Memnite that did is), and the counter
# makes that Memnite a 2/2. With vigilance the Beaver stays untapped and Bot2 takes 4.

